{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"679aeae6c1d37d3369de5d14754f43cdd098a9a5; 7/8 passing (was 3/8). Implemented shallow-push handling in the local push fast path: reject 'shallow update not allowed' when push introduces a new shallow root and receive.shallowupdate is off; when on, pass source grafts to unpack-objects --strict (new UnpackOptions.shallow_boundaries / unpack-objects --shallow-file) so parents of boundary commits aren't required, and append new grafts to the receiver's .git/shallow. New grit-lib/src/shallow.rs helpers new_shallow_roots_for_push + add_shallow_boundaries (with unit tests). Fixed subtests 3,4,5,6. Remaining: subtest 8 'good deltas' — asserts 'Enumerating objects: 5' (we emit 3; git counts delta-base objects during enumeration even with --thin) then exercises pack.usePathWalk=true + test_region pack-objects path-walk; both are pack-objects internals unrelated to shallow push, out of scope. Pre-existing unrelated unit fails: ignore::gitignore_glob_tests (untouched)."}